# PHYTO Reference Sitemap Context

Use this file together with:

- `wordpress-acf-theme-instructions-updated.mdc`
- `wordpress-acf-theme-skill-updated.mdc`
- `selecta-phyto-catalog-project-context.mdc`

This file gives Cursor/agent context about the discovered public structure of `fr.phyto.com` and how to translate that structure into a WordPress catalog-only site.

## Important limitation

The implementation must be a catalog/information adaptation, not a commerce clone.

The reference site includes commerce/account elements, but those are out of scope and must be removed or neutralized:

- Mon compte
- Mon panier
- Add to cart
- Price
- Sale price
- Checkout
- Payment methods
- Shipping claims tied to orders
- Loyalty points
- Customer account flows
- Wishlist/order history
- Product purchase review flows

WordPress admin users are allowed for managing content. Public customer auth is not allowed.

## Discovered top-level site structure

The reference site uses these major public areas:

```text
/
  Homepage

/c/...
  Category / listing pages

/p/...
  Product detail pages

/blog/
  Blog / advice archive

/blog/{article-slug}
  Blog / advice article pages

/cms/{page-slug}
  CMS / landing / legal / brand / campaign pages

/storelocator
  Store locator / points of sale
```

For WordPress, map these to:

```text
/
  front-page.php

/products/
  archive-selecta_product.php

/product/{slug}/
  single-selecta_product.php

/product-category/{term-slug}/
  taxonomy-selecta_product_category.php

/product-line/{term-slug}/
  taxonomy-selecta_product_line.php

/hair-type/{term-slug}/
  taxonomy-selecta_hair_type.php

/hair-concern/{term-slug}/
  taxonomy-selecta_hair_concern.php

/advice/
  archive-selecta_advice.php or a CMS page using an advice query

/advice/{slug}/
  single-selecta_advice.php

/pages/ or normal WordPress pages
  Brand pages, legal pages, campaign pages, FAQ, contact, partners

/store-locator/ or /points-of-sale/
  Partner/store-locator page
```

Use Bulgarian slugs if the client wants localized URLs. Use stable English/internal slugs in code if they simplify development, but public labels should be Bulgarian.

