## Category/listing URL patterns from reference

Reference category URLs often follow this form:

```text
/c/{encoded-id}/{section}/{taxonomy-type}/{slug}
```

Examples discovered:

```text
/c/NzY%3D/soins-de-beaute-et-coiffure/type-de-produit/shampooing
/c/MTUx/soins-de-beaute-et-coiffure/collection/boucles
/c/MTQy/offres-ventes-privees
/c/NzE%3D/soins-de-beaute-et-coiffure/type-de-cheveux/cheveux-secs
/c/chute-de-cheveux/phytophanere-pousse-croissance-cheveux-antichute-post-partum
```

Do not reproduce encoded IDs in WordPress. Use clean semantic slugs.

Recommended WordPress taxonomy routes:

```text
/products/
  All products listing

/product-category/shampoani/
  Product type category

/product-category/balzami-i-maski/
  Product type category

/product-category/stilizanti/
  Product type category

/product-line/boucles/
  Product line/range

/hair-type/suha-kosa/
  Hair type listing

/hair-concern/kosopad/
  Hair concern listing

/promotions/
  Non-commerce promotional/catalog landing page
```

If Bulgarian slugs are preferred, use transliterated Latin slugs for clean URLs and Bulgarian labels in the UI.

